IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cipd-rules`

§ `Tests`

-- Instituted 1 June 2026: sittings from 1 June 2025 count. Served 10 June
-- 2026.
GIVEN sat IS A LIST OF DATE
      prior IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A `Suit`
`a suit over` sat `already penalised` prior MEANS
    `Suit` OF TRUE, sat, Date 1 6 2026, Date 10 6 2026, prior

#ASSERT `the sum I can be made to pay for` (`a suit over` (LIST Date 1 6 2025, Date 5 6 2026) `already penalised` (LIST)) EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the sum I can be made to pay for` (`a suit over` (LIST Date 31 5 2025, Date 5 6 2026) `already penalised` (LIST)) EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the sum I can be made to pay for` (`a suit over` (LIST Date 31 5 2025) `already penalised` (LIST)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the sum I can be made to pay for` (`a suit over` (LIST Date 5 6 2026, Date 10 6 2026, Date 11 6 2026, Date 12 6 2026) `already penalised` (LIST)) EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `the sum I can be made to pay for` (`a suit over` (LIST Date 11 6 2026, Date 12 6 2026) `already penalised` (LIST)) EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `the sum I can be made to pay for` (`a suit over` (LIST Date 11 6 2026, Date 12 6 2026) `already penalised` (LIST Date 12 6 2026)) EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the sum I can be made to pay for` (`Suit` OF FALSE, (LIST Date 11 6 2026), Date 1 6 2026, Date 10 6 2026, (LIST)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT NOT ((`the common informer position for` (`a suit over` (LIST Date 11 6 2026) `already penalised` (LIST)))'s `I can be sued under s 46 of the Constitution`)
